message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. Before publication,
  add the DOI assigned by Zenodo to Version 1.1 (do not reuse the DOI of
  Version 1.0, 10.5281/zenodo.19066947, which identifies a different
  publication) and set the actual date-released.
title: "Interactive Networking Laboratory – Educational Simulators for ISO/OSI, TCP/IP, ARP, DNS, HTTP and Packet Routing"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Capano"
    given-names: "Domenico"
version: "1.1"
# NOTA per l'autore: i campi "doi", "url" e "date-released" sono stati
# rimossi perché non ancora noti per la Version 1.1 (il DOI della
# Version 1.0, 10.5281/zenodo.19066947, NON va riutilizzato qui). Prima
# della pubblicazione definitiva, aggiungere:
#   doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21299699"
#   url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21299699"
#   date-released: "2026-07-10"  (data reale di pubblicazione)
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
abstract: >-
  Interactive Networking Laboratory is a package of interactive,
  dependency-free HTML/JS educational resources for teaching computer
  networking: the ISO/OSI model, TCP/IP architecture, encapsulation, ARP,
  DNS, HTTP, TCP handshake, ICMP/Traceroute, IP fragmentation, and packet
  routing. It includes the main simulator NetLab (internal version 5.5),
  a glossary of terms and network commands, an interactive TCP/IP and
  ISO/OSI concept map with five embedded mini-simulations, and
  documentation for students and teachers. It runs entirely offline in
  the browser, with no installation and no required external
  dependencies.
keywords:
  - ISO/OSI
  - TCP/IP
  - ARP
  - DNS
  - HTTP
  - packet routing
  - computer networking
  - network simulator
  - educational software
  - e-learning
  - Sistemi e Reti
